{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: founding gaps revision 4.2 at f493953ad8680bbdce3bf539c4f3907aacb052d2, all 37 artifacts with packages/room/README.md first. This review carries the completed revision 4 and 4.1 work forward under their replacement request 250b35e1. The migration finding in review 700b74ea and the subsequent recovery and smoke findings are addressed. Earlier token, inventory, binding and delayed-delete fixes remain intact.\n\nArchitecture: Each public founding create owns a durable, unique \u003cbase\u003e-\u003cstep\u003e incarnation; an abandoned attempt is never recreated under its old name. Seal requires the exact holder and no unsettled founding debt. canonical_name routes Room reads, forks, landing, publication and sandbox work to that sealed repository. Destructive effects remain confined to abandoned names, so a delayed old delete cannot destroy the new canonical repository or a subsequent landing.\n\nLegacy public founding is now recognized by a durable registry fact: migration 2 leaves ledger NULL on existing bindings and new binds atomically record 1. Every unfinished public founding reads that fact again, independently of founding_repo and the last bind answer. Workspaces records adoption transactionally and idempotently. Its legacy create remains watched even after absence, deletion or a new seal; an old create can apply again and will still be cleaned. Already-founded rooms return before adoption, and imports bypass newRepository. Fresh bindings with a lost answer or an interrupted first founding do not invent legacy debt.\n\nIndependent actual Worker/DO and SQLite controls: inject a one-shot exception at INSERT INTO artroom_ws_duty for the legacy adoption; the first found refuses, the DO is evicted, retry succeeds and retains one legacy watcher, and a later base-name create is removed with the sealed repository intact. The healthy control also passes. A third control removes ledger from an actual registry table, resets its schema version to 1, evicts it and exercises the constructor's real upgrade: existing binding identity and legacy status survive same-binding retry and a second eviction; a subsequent binding remains nonlegacy. These three controls passed. The same failed-insert control had confirmed the leak on 38057c0a and 42b30aee; it is fixed on this head. This is fault injection, not an assertion that a deployed room suffered a storage failure.\n\nSecurity: Founding uses and durably revokes the creation token rather than issuing another. A complete, validated inventory remains necessary; unknown or malformed inventories cannot establish cleanup. Missing public/import namespace bindings are refused before reservation. Cleanup continues on abandoned incarnations after seal and leaves the sealed repository's ordinary publishing credentials alone. Candidate controls cover existing token-bearing legacy bases, absent bases appearing after seal, repeated appearances, earlier ledger rows, already-founded legacy rooms and recovery windows.\n\nThe smoke now resolves the actual incarnation for its first-commit/ref/read/verify checks and cleans the adopted base, every incarnation and their forks. Three independent controls over the actual cleanupRun and incarnationOf pass: a complete inventory discovers and removes owned repositories even when the canonical incarnation was not previously discovered; malformed and transport-failed inventories clean only known fallback names, remain unknown and fail. Foreign prefix lookalikes survive. No live deploy or credential operation was performed by checker.\n\nSimplification: Keep one durable source for binding provenance and one ledger for unresolved provider effects. This removes the timing-dependent inference from already-bound and founding_repo while preserving the necessary separation between logical identity, sealed storage and abandoned attempts. Nonblocking documentation correction sent to builder: the first adoption bullet in Review 700b74ea still describes the superseded already-bound/no-founding_repo rule; replace it with the registry ledger fact explained by the later recovery paragraph.\n\nValidation: Fresh detached checkout; npm ci installed 374 packages. All workspace type checks passed. Clean exact-head root suite passed 1,692 tests with one skipped, including Git 191 Node, Room 90 Node and 298 workerd. Checker scratch controls were removed before root discovery and are excluded from that count. Separate Git Workers 8 and Git log Workers 11 passed on revision 4, credited here because every Git source/test/config blob is identical. Spike dry build passed: 870.11 KiB, gzip 203.19 KiB. Logs are /tmp/artroom-checker-founding-v42-{ci,types,tests,dry-spike}.log; controls and results are in /tmp/artroom-checker-founding-v42-diagnostics. The first generation attempt for the v4.2 control used an incorrect relative output path, produced no test and was corrected; the successful three-control run is the cited evidence. No implementation source was changed; checkout is clean.\n\nCoverage/integration: The 37 artifacts exactly match changed paths against main 9bb700b6. All seven paths changed from reviewed v4.1 were read; 30 identical artifact blobs were credited to the preceding review work. Whole-tree comparison has 546 identical paths and no deletion. The merge of main preserves amendment 4, bounded-memory publication, deploy cleanup, lane E and pi Workers AI; the combined protocol text and all six both-parent changes were checked during revision 4. The four historical live smoke records were already read; they predate incarnation naming and this revision has not run live. Builder mutation results are not independently reproduced. A coordinated exact-revision public/import/cleanup live proof remains due; this approval is the implementation review and authorizes no separate checker deployment.\n\nFull scope remains: MCP stage 0's cleanup finding, Room amendment 3 concurrency follow-up, amendment 4 runtime publication and large-entry delivery, full pi runtime fa6d295a, and signed proof obligations have their own requests. This review closes only founding implementation b6b51de7; schedule estimates remove no functionality.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e7725a37cc1a4e84760da0ca28746870c21ff54c","binding":"assigned","head":"f493953ad8680bbdce3bf539c4f3907aacb052d2","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ba8158898ac1b1ddc406f3ab3dca0ad35ec3244a\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:da4346a7b787f9370abb6b6abcaadaf010c6334e\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bd72f1975521d3e7295bd1d49784f92ce24b4fc0","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}